  [1mI recommend A.[0m The main thing people need is to find a failed sign-in they don't recognize, and with A that filter is
  one click away. A also uses the existing Select, DatePicker and Search components as specified, and it wraps cleanly
  at 320px. B hides the filters behind an extra click and needs more JavaScript and accessibility work to get through
  review. C takes width away from a table that already has six columns.

  Have a look and tell me what you think here. You can click an option in the browser to select it.

  One housekeeping note: the repo has no [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m, and the sketches are saved under [38;5;153m.hyperpowers/[39m. That folder should
  be ignored. I won't add a [38;5;153m.gitignore[39m without your go-ahead, since it's outside this task.

